  "introduction": {
    "text": "Acquedotto Vergine, also known as Aqua Virgo, is an ancient Roman aqueduct that supplied water to Rome and remains a vital source of water today. Its engineering, longevity, and influence on Roman urban life make it a key cultural landmark.",
